From 9e8f193b84b00a39785e507b12a35fef1e5c9e2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:29:54 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Texture packs: hash = quick computed as PPSSPP computes it

Packs keyed with the format's first hash, quick, were matched to the
game's textures by picture, which cannot find an image the pack redrew
rather than upscaled (a title screen on another background, recoloured
interface pieces). texture_pack_quick_hash() now computes the hash, so a
quick pack's keys find their textures directly, like xxh64 and xxh32
packs.

- The hash's definition was taken as facts (its two forms by length, the
  eight 16-bit starting factors and their step, the order of the
  operations in each 64-byte step) and written here in plain C++ over
  32-bit words; SOURCE_PROVENANCE.md says so.
- <prefix>_QUICK_BY_PICTURE=1 matches quick packs by picture as before;
  <prefix>_NO_QUICK_MATCH=1 still refuses them.
- The import screen no longer says quick packs are matched by picture.
- texture_pack_tests checks the hash at seven lengths against a separate
  model that keeps the state as 16- and 32-bit lanes.

Verified with Dissidia 012 on Windows and a community HD pack (2,324 quick
keys): the redrawn title screen, the first-run Data Config screen and the
main menu replaced (13 images), and 98 of its images in a Quick Battle,
against 4 and 62 matched by picture; texture pack tests pass (MSVC). Not
checked: other games, other quick packs, Linux.
